From: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:39:38 -0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 0/2] usb: xhci: dbc: a network function beside ttyDBC

The xHCI debug capability lets two ordinary PCs talk over a USB 3 debug
cable, with no device controller on either side. Today it can only be
ttyDBC. This RFC adds a second function, dbc_net: a raw IP interface on
the DbC's two bulk rings. The debug host's end is a small usbnet
minidriver (not part of this series), which matches dbc_net by interface
protocol 0, so usb_debug keeps ttyDBC's protocol 1.

Throughput, as iperf3 between the two ends, in Mb/s:

  link                       MTU 9000            MTU 1500
  dbc_net + usbnet driver    900-1650            660-1300
  ttyDBC + userspace bridge  170-230             110-180
  pppd over ttyDBC           -                   60-90

These numbers are from a QEMU emulation of the debug capability, with both
machines in one guest, not from real hardware. They show where the cost
lies, not what a real link will do. Real-hardware results will follow
before a non-RFC posting.

Questions for review:
- Selection. This uses a module parameter, read when a controller is set
  up. A sysfs attribute beside "dbc" is probably better; which would you
  take?
- Kconfig. The tty moves under USB_XHCI_DBGCAP_TTY (default y), and
  USB_XHCI_DBGCAP itself needs only TTY || NET. Tested on x86_64
  defconfig: DBGCAP alone, both functions, and TTY=n with NET.
- Protocol 0 (vendor defined) and the framing: a 4-byte header (magic
  0xdb5e, BE16 length) per packet, as a byte stream. Is there a
  preferred way to identify the function to the host?
- The host driver. A usbnet minidriver for 1d6b:0010 with class dc/02/00
  would go under drivers/net/usb. It is ready, if this direction is
  wanted.

This series is on top of "usb: xhci: dbc: advance the transfer ring's
dequeue pointer", posted separately as a fix. Without it, DbC rings fill
after one lap on kernels since commit 7ee645963075.

Josh Hoffer (2):
  usb: xhci: dbc: let the function undo its own probe
  usb: xhci: dbc: add a network function, dbc_net

